usage: quantfit gate [-h] [--token TOKEN] --baseline BASELINE --quant QUANT
                     (--threshold PP | --tier {smoke,full}) [--eps-upper RATE]
                     [--eps-source STR] [--calibration-report PATH]
                     [--max-new-tokens MAX_NEW_TOKENS] [--report PATH]
                     [--out PATH] [--junit PATH] [--baseline-cache DIR]
                     [--json]

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --token TOKEN         HF token for gated/private models (else uses the
                        HF_TOKEN env)
  --baseline BASELINE, --fp16 BASELINE
                        the unquantized baseline arm
  --quant QUANT         the quantized artifact to gate
  --threshold PP        declared dangerous-axis flip-rate threshold in
                        PERCENTAGE POINTS (e.g. 30 = 30pp)
  --tier {smoke,full}   a named tier instead of a raw threshold
  --eps-upper RATE      per-arm upper bound on BOTH directional judge-error
                        rates (a calibration report's mde_epsilon_upper).
                        Without it the gate prints a perfect-judge FLOOR, not
                        a resolution
  --eps-source STR      where --eps-upper came from (required with it: an
                        unsourced epsilon is not evidence)
  --calibration-report PATH
                        bound schema-2 calibration report; mutually exclusive
                        with --eps-upper/--eps-source. Scope matching does not
                        verify human labels or sensitivity
  --max-new-tokens MAX_NEW_TOKENS
                        completion length per probe (default 64)
  --report PATH         also write the schema-v2 drift report
  --out PATH            write the gate decision artifact JSON
  --junit PATH          also write the gate verdict as JUnit XML: resolution,
                        gated axis and ungated axis as separate cases, so exit
                        5 fails as a refusal rather than as a breached
                        threshold
  --baseline-cache DIR  GGUF pairs only: reuse the baseline arm's completions
                        from DIR when this exact arm, environment, probe set
                        and decode were generated before, and store them when
                        not. A hit skips baseline generation; budgets assume
                        zero hits. Entries hold completion text: local-only,
                        never commit them (*.baseline-cache.json is
                        gitignored)
  --json                emit one JSON document on stdout instead of prose
                        (notices go to stderr)
